cff-version: 1.2.0
message: If you use this software, please cite both the software and the method paper below.
title: FissionTemperatureRatio.jl
abstract: >-
  Extraction of the temperature ratio of complementary fully accelerated fission fragments from
  experimental prompt neutron multiplicity data, independently of any prompt emission model
  calculation, and its parameterization by joined straight segments. Reproduces the total average
  temperature ratios published for 233-U(n,f), 235-U(n,f), 239-Pu(n,f) and 252-Cf(sf).
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Gogîță
    given-names: Paul-Adrian
version: 0.1.0
date-released: "2026-09-13"
license: MIT
repository-code: https://github.com/PaulGoG/FissionTemperatureRatio.jl
keywords:
  - nuclear fission
  - fission fragments
  - prompt neutron multiplicity
  - level density
  - excitation energy partition
  - Julia
references:
  - type: article
    title: >-
      Temperature ratio RT = TL/TH of fully accelerated complementary fragments (used for TXE
      partition) obtained independently of prompt emission model calculations
    authors:
      - family-names: Tudora
        given-names: Anabella
      - family-names: Gogita
        given-names: Paul
    journal: The European Physical Journal A
    volume: 60
    start: 190
    year: 2024
    doi: 10.1140/epja/s10050-024-01375-7
    notes: >-
      The method this package implements. Its equations, conventions and equation numbering are
      the reference for the implementation, and its Tables 1 and 2 are what the validation
      reproduces.
